# Accessibility rollout

Source of truth: `docs/accessibility/UNIFIED_DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`  
Inventory: `docs/accessibility/PORTAL_INVENTORY.md`  
Status: `docs/accessibility/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`

Before any visual or accessibility edit:

1. Read those three files. Do not rely on chat memory.
2. Do only the current stage in the status doc. One stage per chat.
3. Do not restyle a portal already marked IMPLEMENTED or VERIFIED unless the task says to.
4. Clinic desks share `client/src/shared/styles/App.css`. A token or shared-class edit affects every desk. Record that in the status doc.
5. Dashboard tokens live only in `dashboard/src/theme.css`. Do not copy clinic action classes into the dashboard.
6. Update `IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` before finishing.

## Safety

A visual change must not change clinical or financial behavior.

- No schema, API, billing, stock, permission, auth, or routing changes.
- No new CSS framework, component library, or shared UI package.
- Fonts are local `@fontsource` packages only. No Google Fonts or other network font URLs.
- Do not edit unrelated files. Leave other uncommitted work as it is.

Where this spec and `docs/standards/FRONTEND.md` disagree on type, contrast, or target size, the accessibility spec wins. Action roles, overlay class names, bill-rail class names, and F-keys stay in FRONTEND.md.
